    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryson Stott** stands out as our premier option with a score of 72.63. His favorable matchup against R. V\u00e1squez (4.75 xERA) combined with a robust 18% SP Skill bump makes him the clear anchor of the middle infield. **Daulton Varsho** also provides high-leverage value at 63.20; his profile is bolstered by a 10% platoon edge and a subtle 2% boost for targeting a slower delivery, which increases his potential for theft\u2014a critical consideration given our strategy of prioritizing stolen bases in this 5x5 format. While **Gleyber Torres** clears the 60.00 threshold to remain in the lineup, his upside is anchored by a significant 13% dynamic platoon advantage batting out of the lead-off spot against Matz.\n\nThe bench decision for **Masyn Winn** (40.90) proved the most contested. Despite his speed, he was excluded due to a difficult matchup against Eovaldi (3.29 xERA) and negative park factors that neutralized his efficiency relative to the rest of the roster. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding **Luis Arraez** (42.50) and **Matt Chapman** (41.07); both are hovering just above the marginal threshold. Their scores were heavily depressed by a significant 14% penalty for facing a high-skill arm in Harrison, though they retain their spots primarily due to a lack of elite alternatives on the bench today.\n\nManaging our game caps remains a top priority, and we are monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL. We are also tracking the daily utility of bench assets like **Lawrence Butler**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert** to ensure we don't bleed plate appearances on unproductive matchups. With **Yainer Diaz** currently resting, the lineup is optimized to maximize efficiency against these specific pitching profiles, keeping a close watch on potential weather volatility that could impact the high-floor outcomes we expect from **Jonathan Aranda**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Taylor Ward**, and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**.",
